<p><span style="font-family: sans serif;">ti notci la'e lu </span><a class="wiki" href="tiki-index.php?page=le+gusta+co+minde+mutce&bl=y" title="le gusta co minde mutce"><span style="font-family: sans serif;">le gusta co minde mutce</span></a><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> li'u </span></p>
<hr />
<p><a rel="external" href="http://www.kenji-world.net/english/works/texts/restaura.html" target="_blank" class="wiki external"><span style="font-family: sans serif;">Annotation from kenji-world.net</span></a></p>
<p><a rel="external" href="http://tonygonz.blogspot.com/2006/05/restaurant-of-many-orders-miyazawa.html" target="_blank" class="wiki external"><span style="font-family: sans serif;">An unofficial English translation by Tony Gonzalez</span></a></p>
<p><span style="font-family: sans serif;">Ideophones (sa'ei +) </span></p>
<ul>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "kasakasas" from カサカサ (kasakasa) = friction </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "gasagasas" from ガサガサ (gasagasa) = friction </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "za,uaza,uaz" from ザワザワ (zawazawa) = friction </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "pikapikak" from ピカピカ (pikapika) = luster </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "tantaan" from タンターン (tantaan) = shooting </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "kurkur" from クルクル (kurukuru) = rotation </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "douf" from ドウッ (dou-tt) = dashing, pushing </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "vouf" from ボウッ (bou-tt) = hazy </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "gotongoton" from ゴトンゴトン (gotongoton) = rumbling </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "petapetat" from ペタペタ (petapeta) = patting </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "patcin" from パチン (pachin) = snapping </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "patcapatcatc" from パチャパチャ (pachapacha) = splashy </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "gatagatat" from ガタガタ (gatagata) = quivering </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "vurvur" from ブルブル (buruburu) = shivering </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "kiorokioror" from キョロキョロ (kyorokyoro) = shifty eyes </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "kosokosos" from コソコソ (kosokoso) = stealthily </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "kcakcac" from クシャクシャ (kushakusha) = rumpled </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "fufuf" from フフ (fufu) = chuckling </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "uan.uan" from ワンワン (wanwan) = barking </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "guan" from グワン (guwan) = barking </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "fuun" from フーン (fuun) = howling </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "gatar" from ガタリ (gatari) = opening/closing door </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "niaaon" from ニャーオ (nyaao) = meowing </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "xuaan" from クアーン (kuaan) = howling </span></li>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> "gorgor" from ゴロゴロ (gorogoro) = growling, purring </span></li>
</ul>
<p><span style="font-family: sans serif;">Lujvo </span></p>
<ul>
    <li><span style="font-family: sans serif;"> ma'arjipci (cmana jipci) = </span><a rel="external" href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copper_Pheasant" target="_blank" class="wiki external"><span style="font-family: sans serif;">Copper Pheasant</span></a><span style="font-family: sans serif;">, Yama-dori </span></li>
</ul>